    "Additional present-value expenditure is measured against the lowest-spending benchmark over the same observed years. A negative value means the planner spent less than that benchmark. Compare this difference with the physical outcomes, requirement attainment and years in failure; the budget comparison is not a measure of net societal benefit.\n"
   ]
  },
